   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "The compiler errors I have hit with double_exponential under llvm-g++ are not our fault, since I can reproduce the problem just by trying to compile<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/tmp$ cat sign.cpp <br>#include &lt;boost/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">math</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">special_functions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sign</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&lt;iostream&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> main</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cout </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;expect 1, get &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> boost</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">math</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sign</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">endl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cout </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;expect 0, get &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> boost</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">math</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sign</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">endl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cout </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;expect -1, get &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> boost</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">math</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sign</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5.0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">endl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>but we can work around it by defining our own sign() function instead of using boost&#39;s, e.g. this patch<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">diff </span><span style=\"color:#660\">--</span><span style=\"color:#000\">git a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">distributions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">univariate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">double_exponential</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">distributions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">univariate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">double_exponential</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp<br>index ccea83a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">..</span><span style=\"color:#000\">f2c14d2 </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100644</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">---</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">distributions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">univariate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">double_exponential</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+++</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">distributions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">univariate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">continuous</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">double_exponential</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">@@</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">11</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">@@</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">meta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">traits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">constants</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">traits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#800\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">boost</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">math</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">special_functions</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sign</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#800\">//#include &lt;boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> <br> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">namespace</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> <br>   </span><span style=\"color:#008\">namespace</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> prob </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">template</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#008\">typename</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">inline</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">int</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sign</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&amp;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">z </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">?</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> z </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">?</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> <br>     </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// DoubleExponential(y|mu,sigma)  [sigma &gt; 0]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     </span><span style=\"color:#800\">// FIXME: add documentation</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">@@</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">32</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">36</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">@@</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">namespace</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>       </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stan</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">include_summand</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>       </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>       </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> std</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fabs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> boost</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">math</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sign</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\">//     using boost::math::sign; </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>I have not figured out why boost&#39;s implementation of the sign function <br><br><a href=\"http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477591254000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Rsia4fYqTQKh75iYx4RvM\">http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp</a><br><br>is so complicated. I&#39;m sure there is a reason, but I doubt that reason is relevant to Stan. <br><br>With that patch I can get llvm-g++ to pass test-unit and so far it has not broken any other configuration I have tried. I doubt many people would really want to use llvm-g++, but it does get us closer to being able to do on Linux what Xcode does on the Mac, except Xcode is using 4.2.1 and I am using 4.6. Does anyone see a compelling reason to stick with boost&#39;s sign function?<br><br>Ben<br><br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "KylYbbYzRMMJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2012-12-22T23:53:10Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-dev] llvm-g++ and the sign() function",
   "parts": [
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On 12/22/12 3:24 AM, Ben Goodrich wrote:\r<br>&gt; The compiler errors I have hit with double_exponential under llvm-g++ are not our fault, since I can reproduce the\r<br>&gt; problem just by trying to compile\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp$ cat sign.cpp\r<br>&gt; #include &lt;boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp&gt;\r<br>&gt; #include &lt;iostream&gt;\r<br>&gt; int main() {\r<br>&gt;    std::cout &lt;&lt; &quot;expect 1, get &quot; &lt;&lt; boost::math::sign(10.0) &lt;&lt; std::endl;\r<br>&gt;    std::cout &lt;&lt; &quot;expect 0, get &quot; &lt;&lt; boost::math::sign(0.0) &lt;&lt; std::endl;\r<br>&gt;    std::cout &lt;&lt; &quot;expect -1, get &quot; &lt;&lt; boost::math::sign(-5.0) &lt;&lt; std::endl;\r<br>&gt;    return 0;\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; but we can work around it by defining our own sign() function instead of using boost&#39;s, e.g. this patch\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; diff --git a/src/stan/prob/distributions/univariate/continuous/double_exponential.hpp\r<br>&gt; b/src/stan/prob/distributions/univariate/continuous/double_exponential.hpp\r<br>&gt; index ccea83a..f2c14d2 100644\r<br>&gt; --- a/src/stan/prob/distributions/univariate/continuous/double_exponential.hpp\r<br>&gt; +++ b/src/stan/prob/distributions/univariate/continuous/double_exponential.hpp\r<br>&gt; @@ -7,11 +7,15 @@\r<br>&gt;   #include &lt;stan/meta/traits.hpp&gt;\r<br>&gt;   #include &lt;stan/prob/constants.hpp&gt;\r<br>&gt;   #include &lt;stan/prob/traits.hpp&gt;\r<br>&gt; -#include &lt;boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp&gt;\r<br>&gt; +//#include &lt;boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;   namespace stan {\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;     namespace prob {\r<br>&gt; +    template&lt;typename T&gt;\r<br>&gt; +    inline int sign(T&amp; z) {\r<br>&gt; +      return (z == 0) ? 0 : z &lt; 0 ? -1 : 1;\r<br>&gt; +    }\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;       // DoubleExponential(y|mu,sigma)  [sigma &gt; 0]\r<br>&gt;       // FIXME: add documentation\r<br>&gt; @@ -32,7 +36,7 @@ namespace stan {\r<br>&gt;         using stan::prob::include_summand;\r<br>&gt;         using std::log;\r<br>&gt;         using std::fabs;\r<br>&gt; -      using boost::math::sign;\r<br>&gt; + //     using boost::math::sign;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I have not figured out why boost&#39;s implementation of the sign function\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477591256000&amp;usg=AOvVaw01GgdSc2pzLY1f_li01Voj\">http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/boost/math/special_functions/sign.hpp</a>\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; is so complicated.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "It&#39;s Boost --- I think they award a prize to the most obfuscated\r<br>API each year.\r<br>\r<br>And the complex part isn&#39;t even in the above linked file, it&#39;s in\r<br>the traits class that&#39;s included.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br> &gt; I&#39;m sure there is a reason,\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "All they&#39;re doing is using some trait template metaprogramming\r<br>to sort out the floating point representation so that they can mask\r<br>out the sign bit rather than doing a comparison operation.  And do\r<br>efficient sign changes on platforms that support it.\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br> &gt; but I doubt that reason is relevant to Stan.\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "I wish we had efficiency concerns at that level.  But as of now,\r<br>we should just go with Ben&#39;s more straightforward comparison-based code.\r<br>\r<br>(I don&#39;t know what the boundary conditions of sign() are supposed to be for\r<br>NaN given that the return is an int, but I don&#39;t think it matters\r<br>for us one way or another.)\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>&gt; With that patch I can get llvm-g++ to pass test-unit and so far it has not broken any other configuration I have tried.\r<br>&gt; I doubt many people would really want to use llvm-g++, but it does get us closer to being able to do on Linux what Xcode\r<br>&gt; does on the Mac, except Xcode is using 4.2.1 and I am using 4.6. Does anyone see a compelling reason to stick with\r<br>&gt; boost&#39;s sign function?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "Not at all.  Could you just merge that patch into master?\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
