     "On Saturday, December 22, 2012 6:53:10 PM UTC-5, Bob Carpenter wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\nI wish we had efficiency concerns at that level.  But as of now,\n<br>we should just go with Ben&#39;s more straightforward comparison-based code.\n<br>\n<br>(I don&#39;t know what the boundary conditions of sign() are supposed to be for\n<br>NaN given that the return is an int, but I don&#39;t think it matters\n<br>for us one way or another.)\n<br></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><br>Boost&#39;s sign() function returns 1 when given a NaN, which happens to also be what my simple version would do because both comparisons are false.<br><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Not at all.  Could you just merge that patch into master?\n<br></blockquote>"
